  "ai_show_review": {
    "summary": "High‑energy Dark Star suite, soaring Eyes→Stella and tight Weather Report",
    "blurb": "The second set erupts with a monster Dark Star > Mind Left Body Jam sequence, followed by a classic China>Rider and the transcendent Eyes → Stella. Jerry’s solos sparkle on Eyes while Phil lays down deep, thunderous bass throughout. The Weather Report Suite delivers an adventurous climax to an already stellar night.",
    "review": "On October 25, 1973 at Dane County Coliseum the Dead turned in a high‑octane performance that still feels fresh decades later. Set one laid a solid groundwork with tight renditions of Bertha, Here Comes Sunshine and a swinging Playing In The Band, but it was the second set that stole the show. A blistering China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider opened the side, then the band dove into an expansive Dark Star > Mind Left Body Jam > Dark Star Jam that showcases Jerry’s soaring bends and Phil’s thunder‑deep bass lines. Eyes Of The World segued seamlessly into a heartfelt Stella Blue, each note dripping with lyrical nuance. The Weather Report Suite Prelude and Part 1 built a hypnotic groove before the set closed with Let It Grow → Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad and an exuberant One More Saturday Night that let Bob’s vocal flair shine. The encore’s Uncle John’s Band capped a night of relentless improvisational fire, captured best on a crystal‑clear soundboard tape that preserves every nuance of the band’s interplay.",
